// A float narrowed to t128: the interpreter truncates (Rust `as i128`). The JIT
// has no f64 -> i128 conversion and used to PANIC in Cranelift ("Invalid
// OperandSize: 16"); it now refuses cleanly (SKIP).
v: f64 = 300.7
x: t128 = v
y: t64 = x
print(y)
w: f64 = 0.0 - 2.9
z: t128 = w
y2: t64 = z
print(y2)
